 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Your notes mention pre-making round things with a fork.</li><li>Read here as: wetting a bit of the starch and forking it into small crumbs, which stick to the chicken and fry into extra-crunchy nubs.</li><li>Adjust if you did it differently.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "The “round bits”"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>You gave the ingredients, not quantities — these are starting points.</li><li>Taste the marinade: it should be salty-sweet and strongly gingery.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Amounts"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Chicken is safe at <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"74\" data-s=\"0\">74 °C</span></b> in the centre.</li><li>The rest between fries finishes the inside; if unsure, cut the biggest piece open after the second fry.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Is it cooked?"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Never fill the pot more than half full, keep a lid nearby, dry the pieces of excess marinade, and never put water on burning oil.</li><li>Let the oil cool completely before straining or discarding it.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Oil safety"
  }
 ],
